# YAML and plugin config

## plugin.yml
- Commands and permissions must match what the plugin registers in code.
- Document required permissions and usage in comments or docs where appropriate.

## Config YAML
- Preserve existing structure and comments when editing.
- Use the same section layout as in `Plugin/common/src/main/resources/config.yml` and server-specific configs.
- For ServerUPDATE: never commit live secrets; passwords stay `CHANGE_ME` in repo or use `git update-index --skip-worktree` for local values.
